 "standard_url": "https://tea.texas.gov/about-tea/laws-and-rules/sboe-rules-tac/sboe-tac-currently-in-effect/ch111c.pdf",
 "standard_text": "2A.4F solve quadratic and square root equations; 2A.4H solve quadratic inequalities",
 "meta_desc": "Free Algebra II worksheets for Texas TEKS 2A.4F and 2A.4H: solve quadratic equations by square roots and the quadratic formula, complex solutions and quadratic inequalities. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "For ax² + bx + c < 0 with a > 0, the answer is between the zeros.",
 "key_sub": "Take ± when you take a square root.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Square roots: get the square alone, then take ± the square root.</li><li>Quadratic formula: <i>x</i> = <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>−<i>b</i> ± √(<i>b</i><sup>2</sup> − 4<i>ac</i>)</span><span class='fd'>2<i>a</i></span></span>. A negative discriminant gives two complex solutions.</li><li>Quadratic inequality: find the zeros, then test where the parabola is above or below 0.</li><li>For <i>x</i><sup>2</sup> + … &lt; 0 the answer is <b>between</b> the zeros; for &gt; 0 it is <b>outside</b> them.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'><i>x</i><sup>2</sup> − 2<i>x</i> − 8 &lt; 0</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>(<i>x</i> − 4)(<i>x</i> + 2) &lt; 0</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Zeros −2 and 4</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: −2 &lt; <i>x</i> &lt; 4</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>(<i>x</i> − 3)<sup>2</sup> = 12</p><p class='sn-ex-s'><i>x</i> − 3 = ±2√3</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: <i>x</i> = 3 ± 2√3</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Forgetting ±</td><td><i>x</i><sup>2</sup> = 9 gives 3 and −3.</td></tr><tr><td>Inside instead of outside</td><td>&gt; 0 means outside the zeros (for <i>a</i> &gt; 0).</td></tr><tr><td>Not reversing the sign</td><td>Multiplying by a negative reverses the inequality.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
